.TH SIGNALFD 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
signalfd \- Linux x86-64 syscall 289
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_260_299.h>
.B int signalfd(int descriptor, const sigset_t* mask, int flags);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates or updates a signal descriptor with flags and an eight-byte kernel signal mask.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR signalfd (2)
